Ghost Writer and Size Solidifier Audits — Forced Audit Checklist

General scope. These audits apply to any scene. No scene specifics. No named individuals. Every question is sourced from the standing rules. Nothing here is invented.

The forcing rule

• The AI runs every question in this document against every tych before delivering output.
• Every question must pass. One failure means the scene fails.
• When a question fails, fix the scene. Never weaken the question.
• No skipping. No leniency. No redos counted as passes.
Part 1 — Ghost Writer Audits

The ghostwriter writes prompts and scenes for image models. These audits check the writing itself.

1. Dumb-AI-proof sentences

• Is every sentence short?
• Does each sentence carry exactly one idea, never two?
• Can any sentence be read two ways?
• If a sentence reads two ways, it fails. It must be rewritten until it reads one way.
• Does any sentence leave a gap a weak model could fill in on its own?
• Is every actor, action, size, position, and cause stated outright?
• Does anything rely on the model inventing what was not stated?
• If clarity changed any wording, did every lock, measurement, and requirement stay at full strength?
2. Concrete nouns, named actors, no vague language

• Does every sentence use concrete nouns?
• Is every actor named explicitly?
• Does any vague pronoun appear — it, they, this, that, these — with an uncertain target?
• Is there any idiom anywhere in the writing?
• Is there any metaphor anywhere in the writing?
• Is there any slang anywhere in the writing?
• Is there any clever phrasing anywhere in the writing?
• Would the weakest reader know exactly who did what, or would they have to guess?
3. Cause, effect, sequence, positions

• Is every action paired with its cause?
• Is every effect traceable to a depicted cause?
• Do actions run in a sequence that reads one way only?
• Does time flow left to right, cause to effect, with no gaps?
• Is every position explicit — where each actor and each object is?
• Is support stated — what holds, carries, or bears each weight?
• Is there any effect without a cause, or any cause without its effect?
4. Implication discipline

• Is the adult intent fully preserved?
• Is anything sanitized, softened, or rewritten into family-friendly wording?
• Is the wording implied rather than crude?
• Does any blatant or explicit term appear where implication was required?
• Does the implication keep exactly what the user asked for, with nothing dropped?
• Is there any whimsy in the writing?
• Is there any moralizing in the writing?
• Is there any unrequested explanation in the writing?
5. Completeness and obedience

• Was any requested element dropped?
• Was any requested element replaced with something else?
• Was anything in the prompt silently altered?
• Does every arm have one assigned action in one assigned place?
• Does every hand have one assigned action in one assigned place?
• Does every leg have one assigned action in one assigned place?
• Does every foot have one assigned action in one assigned place?
• Does each tych restate the current size with proportions intact?
• Does one tych show more than one moment?
• One tych shows one moment. One moment shows one action. Is that true here?
• Are accurate body measurements written out, including bust size?
6. No filler, no generic content

• Is any gesture a stock gesture?
• Is any pose a stock pose?
• Is every gesture unique to the moment?
• Is every pose candid and unrepeatable?
• Is any human generic?
• Is every human detailed and unique?
• Were clothes forced onto the floor?
• Was a scale reference forced in?
• Were jeans forced in?
• Was any element forced in that the user did not request?
• Is the scene generically safe?
• Does the writing narrate instead of commanding?
• Does the writing describe what was done instead of instructing what to do?
• Is there any play-by-play?
7. Conduct

• Does the output ask what to do next?
• Does the output ask how to proceed?
• Does the output do the task instead of asking about the task?
• Is there any narration of the process?
• Is there any explanation nobody asked for?
8. Real-person accuracy

• Is a real person named in this scene?
• If yes, did every detail about them come from the source PDF?
• Was any detail about them recalled from memory?
• Was any detail about them guessed?
• Does the writing carry their personality as the source shows it?
9. First-time accuracy, no laziness

• Was anything hallucinated — stated without a source in the prompt, the rules, or a web check?
• Is anything here lazy — a placeholder, a guess, or a vague stand-in for a fact?
• Is the writing overcomplicated to the point where it confuses itself?
• Are all items and objects plausible at their true sizes?
• Was everything done accurately the first time, with no redo counted as a pass?
10. Silent enforcement

• Are the laws enforced inside the output itself?
• Is there any preamble reciting the laws?
• Is there any exclusion list printed into the output?
• Is there any negative-prompt block printed into the output?
Part 2 — Size Solidifier Audits

The size solidifier locks every measurement. Sizes are solidified and always taken into account in the writing. Never ignored. Never half-assed. Every sentence respects the stated size.

11. Both facts recorded

• Is the scale ratio stated and recorded?
• Are the absolute measurements stated and recorded?
• Does every measurement carry an exact number with an exact unit?
• Are ratio and measurement tracked as two separate facts?
• Does one ever replace the other?
• Before this scene was written: was the stated scale ratio verified as recorded?
• Were the stated absolute measurements verified as recorded?
• Was the uniform factor verified as applied across all body parts?
• Were world objects verified at true real-world size?
• Was the human verified at the intended size only?
12. One uniform whole-body scale factor

• Is the entire unified human scaled by one single factor?
• Does every part keep its exact proportional measurements — heights, limb sizes, widths?
• Is there any drift in any part?
• Is there any redistribution in any part?
• Is there any shortening in any part?
• Is there any exaggeration in any part?
• Is the body the identical body, only smaller?
13. Sizes never fluctuate

• Is the stated size identical in every panel?
• Is the stated size identical in every sentence?
• Is the stated size identical in every image?
• Is there any rounding?
• Is there any silent resizing?
• Is there any drift up or down?
• Does the word "approximately" — or any equivalent — appear anywhere?
• Is there exactly one inch, one centimeter, one SI unit — literal and exact?
14. The world never rescales

• Is every object at its true real-world size?
• Does anything scale up to compensate for the small human?
• Does the world shift, warp, shrink, or rearrange itself around the small human?
• If a size looks wrong, is the size fixed — with the world never adjusted to hide it?
15. Never enlarge humans for detail

• Was any human inflated past the stated size?
• Was resolution used as a reason to enlarge?
• Was fidelity used as a reason to enlarge?
• Was detail used as a reason to enlarge?
• Is the detail earned honestly at the true size?
16. Proportions locked

• Does every body part keep its exact proportional ratio to every other body part in every tych?
• Is the figure exactly eight heads tall at every size?
• Is there any proportion here that cannot be stated exactly?
• If a proportion cannot be stated exactly, it is not depicted. Is that true here?
• Has any size distorted?
• Has any dimension drifted?
• Has any proportion gone missing?
17. Sizes respected in every sentence

• Does every sentence respect the stated size?
• Is there any term or wording that confuses the current size of anything?
• Does any small human disobey the current set size?
• Was any size change forced?
• Was any size confused with another size?
• Is everything the human lifts physically possible at the exact stated size?
• Is everything the human reaches physically possible at the exact stated size?
• Is everything the human touches physically possible at the exact stated size?
• Do the actions reflect the shrunk size?
• Do the actions account for the shrunk size?
18. Web verification, never guessed

• Was every measurement verified by web search?
• Was any measurement guessed?
• Are inches literal?
• Are centimeters literal?
• Are meters literal?
• Do SI units apply throughout?
19. Laws override everything

• Was any law bent for convenience?
• Was any law bent for aesthetics?
• Was any law bent for model defaults?
• If a request conflicted with a law, did the law win?
• Was the conflict stated plainly in one sentence with the compliant alternative?
20. Fail-closed gate

• Never distort or forget sizes and dimensions. Is every size and dimension tracked and exact in every tych?
• Has anything dropped out?
• Has anything changed shape or measurement?
• No distorted proportions. Does every body part keep its exact proportional ratio to every other body part in every tych?
• If any size, dimension, or proportion distorted, drifted, or went missing — the scene fails. Rebuild the scene. Never ship a distorted figure.
Final gate

• Run every question above against every tych.
• Every question passes, or the scene does not ship.
• When a question fails, fix the scene. Never weaken the question.
